{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "label": "Mailbox sizing (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "label": "The unbounded default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An actor framework cannot know which of your messages is expendable, and between v0.10 and v0.15 this one guessed: every mailbox was bounded at 10 000 with drop-head, which is right for a sensor reading and wrong for a Terminated signal, a delivery confirmation or a WebSocket close \u2014 all three became filed defects. The ceiling that bought was not even real, since only the user queue was bounded."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_backlog_warning_threshold", "label": "Growth you are told about", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A queue reaching 10 000 logs a warning and again at each doubling, always on and needing no metrics stack, so heap exhaustion announces itself well before it arrives."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_death_watch_lane", "label": "The death-watch lane no bound can shed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A Terminated now arrives through a lane no overflow policy can shed and no throttle can drop, so a bound you set costs the actor its backlog and never the deaths it is watching for; the WebSocket connection-spawn command is covered the same way."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_boundedmailbox", "label": "BoundedMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three patterns justify one: a producer/consumer mismatch known in advance, telemetry where stale data is wrong, and a critical actor near its limits."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_overflow_policies", "label": "The three overflow policies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pick by what the right answer is on overflow: reject where the sender should retry or alert, drop-head where stale data is wrong, drop-new where queued work is precious. There is no best \u2014 it is context-dependent."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_picking_capacity", "label": "Picking a capacity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three factors: worst-case burst size, per-message memory (capacity x bytes bounds the cost) and latency budget (capacity / drain rate bounds the wait). Capacities below the natural burst size make reject fire on normal traffic."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_depth_is_not_a_throughput_problem", "label": "Depth is not a throughput problem", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both queues are ring buffers, so a queue of a million costs the same per message as a queue of ten; what a deep queue costs is memory and latency, and neither is fixed by a faster queue."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_reading_the_metrics", "label": "Reading the mailbox metrics", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Size is the presence signal with the path, depth is the distribution to size a capacity from since its p99 measures the burst a capacity bets on, wait is the earlier signal and the one to alert on, and dropped_total is by design for the actors you bounded and should not appear anywhere else."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_prioritymailbox", "label": "PriorityMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lower numbers are higher priority and system messages always trump; for HTTP responses against batch jobs, or health pings against bulk metrics."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_priority_with_bound", "label": "Priority and a bound together", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "drop-head is absent on purpose, because a priority queue head is the message you called most important; drop-lowest-priority sheds from the other end, which is the version of shedding a priority mailbox exists to express. A message whose priorityFor cannot be evaluated is ranked last, so a broken callback shows up as a rising drop rather than an error unless you wire onPriorityError."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_blanket_bounding_hazard", "label": "Blanket-bounding every actor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bound is a decision to discard messages and can only be made where someone knows which ones are expendable; applied across the board it reaches actors nobody assessed and the evicted envelope is a control message \u2014 which is the shape the unbounded default exists to prevent."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_backpressure_layering", "label": "Mailbox as one layer of backpressure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mailbox enforces the local boundary; sender retry logic and upstream rate-limiting (HTTP 429, broker push-back) are the rest, and no bound fixes a handler that is simply too slow."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_backlog_warning_threshold", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_death_watch_lane", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_boundedmailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_boundedmailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_overflow_policies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_picking_capacity", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_boundedmailbox", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_depth_is_not_a_throughput_problem", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_do